+\begin{lemma}[Multiplicativity of $\chi$ across formal direct
+sums]\label{lem:chi-multiplicative}
+Let $L_1, L_2$ be scalar linear operators on $\mathbb{C}[x]$ each
+with a single irregular singularity at $x = \infty$ and Newton polygon
+a single edge of slope $-p_\alpha / q_\alpha$ ($\alpha = 1, 2$), with
+$p_1/q_1 \ne p_2/q_2$. Let $L_{12}$ be any scalar operator realising
+the formal direct sum $\widehat{M}(L_1) \oplus \widehat{M}(L_2)$ via
+a cyclic vector. Then
+$\chi_{L_{12}}(c) = \chi_{L_1}(c)\,\chi_{L_2}(c)$.
+\end{lemma}
+
+\begin{proof}
+The Newton polygon of a formal direct sum of irregular connections is
+the upper convex hull of the Newton polygons of the summands
+(\cite[Ch.~III]{sabbah-isomon}; \cite[Ch.~II]{robba-malgrange}); for
+distinct slopes it has two edges. On the edge $E_\alpha$ at slope
+$-p_\alpha/q_\alpha$ in $N(L_{12})$ only the summand
+$\widehat{M}(L_\alpha)$ contributes leading-order $\LCinf$-data
+(the other summand has formal type of strictly different slope and
+contributes only sub-leading corrections). Hence the per-edge
+characteristic polynomial of $L_{12}$ on $E_\alpha$ coincides with
+$\chi_{L_\alpha}$. The total $\chi_{L_{12}}$ is the product of its
+per-edge polynomials, giving
+$\chi_{L_{12}}(c) = \chi_{L_1}(c)\,\chi_{L_2}(c)$.
+\end{proof}
